<p>A Vatican appeals court has thrown out the original indictment against Cardinal Giovanni Angelo Becciu and ordered a new trial, ruling that procedural errors undermined the original proceedings. One report said Becciu’s previously imposed prison sentence remains in place pending the retrial, underscoring that the appeal did not end the case.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/99dW4LFhKvjgSNomWmkI3UuBVltChXnU9Pauj2QD9zkbflirgFp9gFZ50VfwtriuuDKftneUzuZR1YawNTjz4puIKq03X_v4BX8RoeZ42bwictyAFr7-eobT1jVb3l-_K1WuDY0_1ksuRizQbNwBhSI6GiypSJHxkJtZFluJ1cLTtUtWUY9RVaI' alt='Cardinal Giovanni Angelo Becciu at the Vatican in 2024.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Historic first: The case drew unusual attention because Becciu became the first cardinal ever convicted by the Vatican’s criminal court in 2023.</li><li>Why it mattered: Multiple outlets said the proceedings were widely described as the Vatican’s “trial of the century,” reflecting intense scrutiny of the Holy See’s finances.</li><li>A landmark case: DW described the matter as a landmark fraud case, highlighting why the appeals ruling carries weight beyond Becciu himself.</li><li>What the retrial is about: GMA said Becciu was convicted of embezzlement, emphasizing that the new trial still centers on alleged financial wrongdoing.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Vatican appeals tribunal: PBS reported that the tribunal blamed both Pope Francis and Vatican prosecutors for procedural errors that compromised the original case. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/vatican-appeals-tribunal-declares-mistrial-in-trial-of-the-century-against-cardinal'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Cardinal Angelo Becciu: Becciu kept pressing his appeal, using the procedural ruling in his effort to overturn the judgment against him. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/vatican-declares-partial-mistrial-in-cardinal-s-fraud-case/a-76400048'>DW</a>)</li><li>Vatican court system: By sending the allegations back for a new round instead of discarding them, the court signaled that it still wants the case tested under cleaner procedures. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/17/world/europe/vatican-cardinal-retrial.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/vatican-declares-partial-mistrial-in-cardinal-s-fraud-case/a-76400048'>Vatican declares partial mistrial in cardinal&#x27;s fraud case</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/vatican-appeals-tribunal-declares-mistrial-in-trial-of-the-century-against-cardinal'>Vatican appeals tribunal declares mistrial in &#x27;trial of the century&#x27; against cardinal</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/17/world/europe/vatican-cardinal-retrial.html'>Tribunal Calls for Retrial of the Vatican’s ‘Trial of the Century’</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/topstories/world/980389/vatican-court-orders-embezzlement-re-trial-for-cardinal/story/'>A Vatican appeals court orders a retrial of Cardinal Giovanni Angelo Becciu, who was convicted of embezzlement in 2023, citing procedural errors in the original proceedings. The court maintains his previously imposed prison sentence pending the outcome of the new trial.</a> - gmanetwork.com</li></ul>